    {
      "article_id": "ART003277431",
      "id": "ART003277431",
      "kci_id": "ART003277431",
      "title_kr": "唐宋宗教之變: 瑜伽密教影響下中國宗教新格局的確立",
      "title_en": "The Religious Transformation in the Tang and Song Dynasties: The Establishment of a New Religious Landscape in China under the Influence of Yoga and Tantric Buddhism",
      "authors": [
        {
          "name": "戴曉雲",
          "affiliation": "中國傳媒大學",
          "order": "1"
        }
      ],
      "abstract_kr": "瑜伽密教即指唐代密宗, 有理密和事密(法事), 在唐代, 瑜伽密教稱為瑜伽教, 事密稱為瑜伽教法. 會昌法難, 瑜伽密教理密喪盡僅存事密, 即是瑜伽教法, 明代称为瑜伽教. 瑜伽教法對唐代以降的中國宗教發展產生了重要影響, 是理解唐宋以降中國宗教發展變化的關鍵. 宋元新道教(法)ㆍ民間宗教等均與瑜伽教法關係密切; 水陸法會是瑜伽教法的一種, 也稱為水陸法. 唐宋以降中國宗教新格局確立, 華夏文化在儒釋道三教彼此交融中創新和發展.",
      "abstract_en": "Yoga Tantra refers to the Esoteric Buddhism of the Tang Dynasty, which includes both theoretical and practical aspects (ritual practices). During the Tang Dynasty, Yoga Tantra was called Yoga Teaching, and practical aspects were called Yoga Teaching Method. During the Huichang Persecution of Buddhism, the theoretical aspect of Yoga Tantra was almost entirely lost, leaving only the practical aspect, which is Yoga Teaching Method, known as Yoga Teaching in the Ming Dynasty. Yoga Teaching Method had a significant impact on the development of Chinese religion from the Tang Dynasty onwards and is key to understanding the changes in Chinese religion from the Tang and Song Dynasties onwards. The Neo-Taoism (or Taoism) of the Song and Yuan Dynasties and folk religions were closely related to Yoga Teaching Method; the Water and Land Ritual is a type of Yoga Teaching Method, also known as the Water and Land Ritual. From the Tang and Song Dynasties onwards, a new religious landscape was established in China, and Chinese culture innovated and developed through the integration of Confucianism, Buddhism, and Taoism.",
